## Contract (raw bpy module; the harness builds it once and the zones instance it)
{{ frame_doc }}
{{ contract }}
- `{{ asset_file }}` must define `def build_{{ asset_file.rsplit('/', 1)[-1][:-3] }}(ctx, variant=0)` that links
  every part into `ctx.collection` (its own Collection, pre-made and active) and returns it: built at
  the origin, lowest point on z = 0, footprint centred on the origin, front facing −Y, sized as stated
  (±5 %).  Zone code places collection instances of `ctx.assets['{{ asset_file.rsplit('/', 1)[-1][:-3] }}']` by
  that origin and never calls you.
- Build from bmesh (`create_cube` / `create_cone` / `create_icosphere` / `create_circle`, scaled and
  translated) and Principled materials with colours (`Base Color`, `Roughness`, `Metallic`; a noise
  bump; `lib/materials.py` has the palette) — several parts with distinct materials, each a uniquely
  named PascalCase object (one root mesh, or children parented under it with a RELATIVE location).
- `variant` (0..n) and `ctx.rng(seed)` may vary details deterministically; `random.*` is a lint error.
- Segments 10–24; at most 15000 triangles for the whole asset (it is instanced).
- No lights, no cameras, no world, no `bpy.ops` in loops, no file IO; nothing outside the asset
  itself (no ground plane).
- MOTION (only when the description names a moving part — a swinging lamp, a turning wheel): keyframe
  that part's OWN rotation/location on `ctx.frame(0.0)` and `ctx.frame(1.5)` (LINEAR), or a simple
  driver of `frame` (`frame * 0.2`); put the part's origin at its pivot.  Amplitude must read at scene
  distance (≥ 0.15 rad or ≥ 0.05 m).
