## DO / DON'T
- DO use the exact size numbers above; the zone builders and the placement gate rely on them.
- DO give it the 3–4 recognisable features a person would name (a stone lantern: base, post, light
  box with 4 windows, curved roof, finial) — plus 2–3 pieces of wear or incident that make it look
  used: a chipped corner, a leaning post, moss at the base, a rope, a hanging tool.
- DO make `variant` (0..n) change the SILHOUETTE, not just the scale: at least 3 visibly different
  versions (a different crown shape, a different roof pitch, a broken vs whole rail).  Zones rely on
  this for variety, so a `variant` that only scales is a wasted asset.
- DO give any repeated natural asset per-instance hue room: vary the colour from `variant` /
  `ctx.rng(seed)` so 20 copies are not one colour.
- DON'T model a flat plane with a colour where the thing has real thickness (a fence is stakes and
  rails, not a textured quad) — closeups are judged.
- DON'T leave floating pieces: every sub-shape overlaps a neighbour by ≥ 2 mm, and the lowest point
  is exactly z = 0 (the harness measures a part sunk below it or hovering above it).
- DON'T write anything outside the listed file.
